# Rust
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Data pool, shards, checkpoints — large, reproducible from manifests.
# The manifests themselves ARE tracked: they are the provenance record.
#
# `/data/pool/` alone did NOT do that. git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory
# is excluded, so every manifest under it was ignored too and the comment above described
# an intention with no mechanism. The `/**` form excludes the CONTENTS rather than the
# directory, which is what makes the negations below reachable.
/data/pool/**
!/data/pool/**/
!/data/pool/**/manifest.json
!/data/pool/*.manifest.json
/data/shards/
/data/checkpoints/
*.npy.gz
*.safetensors
*.bin

# Never commit credentials or environment files.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*-service-account*.json

# Container build logs. The lockfile and Containerfile are tracked; their output is not.
# AUDIT/ holds the *analysis* — the .md files and clones.json are the evidence record, and
# they quote the specific log lines any claim rests on. The raw logs themselves are not
# tracked, for the same reason stack/.build.log is not.
stack/.build.log
AUDIT/*.log

# The DevMap code-intelligence index: generated, binary, 15 MB, and rebuilt in 186 ms by
# `devmap build .`. It is derived state, not provenance.
.devmap/

# DevCouncil's local ledger: 4.7 MB of SQLite plus a live -wal, rewritten continuously by
# whichever sessions are attached. Same reasoning as .devmap/ above — derived state, and a
# binary that would conflict on every parallel run. The decision record this repo keeps is
# ledger/ (JSONL, append-only, tracked) and gaps.jsonl, not this.
.devcouncil/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# The ledger is append-only and IS tracked — it is the decision record.
# Nothing under ledger/ is ignored.
